  "semantics": [
    "Default backend is CPU, including a Vulkan-enabled build. Vulkan requires Cargo asr-vulkan plus explicit --asr-backend vulkan; unsupported build choices fail before model loading.",
    "ASR uses selected backend; Silero VAD remains CPU. Existing model, phrase worker, incremental conv stem and prompt-prefix cache paths remain unchanged.",
    "C/Rust config appends one int32 backend; library STAMP requires backend and config-abi=2 to reject a stale pre-change native archive. Both halves must rebuild together.",
    "Separate native/aarch64 CPU and Vulkan output directories. Static backend and dependency link order explicit; Vulkan loader is a linked runtime dependency.",
    "Pinned transcribe source unchanged. Private app CMake attaches existing SPIRV-Headers imported include target after initial missing-header failure."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Host x86_64 build/link only, not A53 cross-build or runtime performance.",
    "No GPU/ASR inference, model conversion, tablet deployment or service changes.",
    "Current qualified Radish cannot yet satisfy pinned ggml hard storageBuffer16BitAccess/VK_KHR_16bit_storage and Vulkan1.2 SPIR-V/device environment; no check bypass or feature inflation.",
    "Source/config intent is not evidence of current deployed process backend."
  ],
